# Mobile screen layout consistency

Tab roots and stack screens share one top chrome and one page-body gutter. Do not invent a
per-screen inset under the title bar.

## Top chrome

- Use **`HeaderBar`** for the slot under the status bar: safe-area inset and a 44pt row. No
  divider, hairline, or shadow under the title.
- Stack titles go through **`ThemedStackHeader`** (already wraps `HeaderBar` via
  **`HeaderBarChrome`**). Trailing header actions use **`HeaderBarAction`** in `headerRight` —
  do not invent a one-off top-right `Pressable`. A header More opens **`MoreMenu`** — a bottom
  sheet that appears instantly: tertiary action group with centered bold rows, then a
  separate opaque quaternary Cancel block (same bold weight). Do not slide or fade, do
  not use a translucent Cancel fill, do not use a centered card, and do not style Cancel
  as a pill.
- Tab roots use the same title slot (Home, Search, …). Page controls such as Home's media-type
  pills and Search's field and chips sit in the body under that bar, not inside it.

## Page body under the bar

The first content below `HeaderBar` uses **`screenBodyInsets(tokens.spacing)`** from
`apps/mobile/src/theme/screenLayout.ts`:

- **Top:** `spacing.lg` between the title row and the first body control
- **Horizontal:** `spacing.lg` on both sides of that body

`MobileScreenContainer` already applies this. Home's feed list and Search's field / chips / list
must use the same helper — not a one-off `padding` / `margin`, and not a second inner `Card`
padding on top of the page gutter.

Screen lists (Home, Search, Library, …) are unboxed: no perimeter `Card` around the rows. `Card`
is a surface for grouped settings or section chrome, not for a scrolling result list.

Internal gaps stay on the screen. Prefer one column **`gap`** for a stack of related controls so
spaces stay equal by construction (Search: field → chips → list rule all share `spacing.base`).
**Spacing symmetry:** when two sides of a control should feel like the same relationship (above
and below chips, around a divider, between paired labels), use the same token — do not mix
`base` on one side and `md` on the other. Centered empty / loading (`VerticalCenter`,
`CallToActionSection`, `LoadingSection`) fills leftover height; it does not replace the page gutter.

## Search field and chips

Search uses **`SearchField`** (built on **`TextField`**): tertiary fill, no resting outline,
leading magnifying-glass, a 2px transparent border that becomes `tokens.border.primary` on
focus. Do not restyle a bare `TextInput` with a perimeter stroke.

The painted pill is the hit target. A tap anywhere inside it — padding, empty space, or the
leading glass — focuses the input. `TextField` implements that; do not rebuild it per screen.
Do not enlarge the area by adding padding on the `TextInput` (that moves the placeholder).
Submit stays on the keyboard return key. Leaving the screen blurs the field — do not keep a
caret or focus ring across a tab switch. Focus again only when the user taps or a screen
explicitly requests it (`autoFocus`). The same contract applies to other painted controls you
touch: the visible shape is what the finger can press.

Two or three filters under a field use **`OptionChipGroup`**. Selected chip = `buttonPrimary` fill.
Settings density (2–3 chips vs option-list screen) is **mobile-settings-option-density**.

Standalone cover art uses **`CoverImage`**, which opens **`ImageViewerModal`** on tap. Pass
**`viewerUri`** from **`primaryLightboxArtworkUrl`** (or the channel variant) so the modal loads the
largest original, not the list thumb. Do not add a nested image tap when the parent row, cell, or
header is already the pressable control (`opensViewer={false}`). Resolve display `uri` with
**`primaryListArtworkUrl`** — see **header-hero-image-sources**. The app stays portrait; the viewer
does not unlock landscape.

## Hub menus

More, Library, and Browse use **`MenuListScreen`**. A section title sits **above** its `Card`
(`tokens.text.accent`, heading weight) with `spacing.lg` before the card and `spacing.xl`
between groups. Rows that push a screen show a `›`. In-place actions (Log out) set
`showsChevron: false`. Skip empty sections. More Account includes Login / Sign up or Log out.

## List rows

Media and result rows use **`HomeFeedRow`** (or **`ListRow`** when the layout is title/subtitle
only). Vertical padding uses **`listRowVerticalPadding(tokens.spacing.base)`** from
`apps/mobile/src/theme/screenLayout.ts`: top is the token, bottom is top plus
**`LIST_ROW_OPTICAL_BOTTOM_EXTRA`** (2). That extra offsets system-font line-box bias so title ink
does not read top-heavy — apply on text-bearing row containers only, not every `Text`, grid tiles,
or icon-only rows. Row artwork is **`LIST_ROW_ARTWORK_SIZE`** (60). Space between title, subtitle,
and other in-row lines with a column **`gap`** (`spacing.sm`) — not `marginTop` /
`marginBottom` on each line — so a missing subtitle or metadata line adds no leftover space. The
text stack uses `justifyContent: 'center'` so it stays vertically centered on the artwork. The gap
between artwork and text is **`listRowArtworkGap(tokens.spacing)`** (`spacing.base`) — same helper
for `HomeFeedRow`, `ListRow`, and `MiniPlayer` — not a per-screen `spacing.md` or a leading
`marginLeft`. Channel headers use a wider art→title gap (`spacing.lg`) because the mark is 78px.

Icon-only controls share **`LIST_ROW_ACTION_SIZE`** (44) and bare glyphs use
**`LIST_ROW_ACTION_ICON_SIZE`** (26); Play’s triangle uses **`LIST_ROW_PLAY_ICON_SIZE`** (16)
inside the glowing `play` Button. Prefer Button `variant="play"` for the media-row Play circle and
`variant="ghost"` for bare More; Download/trash stay borderless at the same hit target.

Under a channel header, **`listHeaderStackGap(tokens.spacing)`** (`spacing.lg`) is the gap
**above** the chip row (header → chips). Do not mix `md` on one seam and `lg` on another for that
header stack.

## Chip row → next block

Space **below** a **`SectionChipRow`** (Home / Browse media types, podcast sections) is
**`listChipRowBottomGap(tokens.spacing)`** (`spacing.base`). It is applied as the row's own
`paddingBottom` inside `SectionChipRow` — do **not** add a second `paddingBottom` /
`marginTop` on the screen wrapper (Home/Browse `selectorSection`, podcast filter `marginTop`,
About surface `marginTop`) or the seam doubles or disappears when the next sibling changes.

Whatever follows the chips (filter field, episode list, about prose, podroll) inherits that same
gap. Filter fields then use **`listFilterFieldBottomMargin`** for the filter→row seam only.

## Filter field → content seam

The gap from a **`ListFilterField`** bottom edge to the first list row or grid tile is
**`listFilterContentGap(tokens.spacing)`** (`spacing.base`). Apply it with
**`listFilterFieldBottomMargin(tokens.spacing, nextContentTopPadding)`** as the field's
`marginBottom`:

- **List** rows that use `listRowVerticalPadding(spacing.base)`: pass `spacing.base` so the field
  does not double the row's top padding.
- **Grid** tiles with no top padding: pass `0`.

Do not use a raw `marginBottom: spacing.md` on the filter (too tight on grid once list padding is
added elsewhere, too loose on list when stacked with row padding). Home switches the second
argument with `isGridView` so both view modes share one seam.

Row dividers are `StyleSheet.hairlineWidth` + `themeStyles.border.borderColor`. The **last row
omits the bottom border** so a hairline does not sit on the list edge. Pass `isLast` on
`HomeFeedRow`. `ListSection` already supplies it as the third `renderItem` argument
`(item, index, isLast)`. `ReorderableSections` uses the same last-row rule.

The rule between chips/filters and the first row is one step stronger than a row hairline:
`height: 1`, the same `themeStyles.border.borderColor`, and horizontal inset from
`screenBodyInsets().paddingHorizontal` (Search's `listRule`). Do not invent a second color.

## Fill empty lists do not scroll

When a list's only body is a fill info state (`VerticalCenter` / `LoadingSection` /
`CallToActionSection` / **`ListEmpty`** as `ListEmptyComponent`), there is nothing to scroll. Use
**`FillList`** instead of raw `FlatList` — it locks bounce, over-scroll, pull-to-refresh, and
`scrollEnabled` whenever `data` is empty and `ListEmptyComponent` is set.

**`ListEmpty`** wraps **`VerticalCenter`** and uses **`typography.subheading`** (same scale as
`CallToActionSection` message copy) so "no results" / "nothing here" lines up across screens.

Podcast section lists use **`PodcastSectionList`**, which already composes **`FillList`** +
**`ListEmpty`**.

## Podcast detail filter visibility

Show **`ListFilterField`** only when **`isFilterableSection(section)`** is true
(`podcastSections.ts`). Clips and podroll are **not** filterable — clips are server-paginated, and
podroll is a short publisher list without title filtering. Episodes, official soundbites, and
**Downloaded** are filterable.

**Downloaded** is always offered (last chip): it lists finished offline episodes for this channel
from `downloadsRepository.listCompleteByChannel`. An empty list is a real answer.

Sort **`MenuSelectChip`** stays mounted on every section. On non-sortable tabs (About, Podroll,
soundbites) pass **`disabled`** so the face grays out and does not open — do not unmount it, or the
section pills jump. When `sort === 'top'`, keep the range chip mounted the same way (also
`disabled` when the section is not sortable).

## Action-gated account / membership

When the screen is usable and one control is gated, keep the control visible. On press, call
`useMembershipGate().openGate(reason)` so `ConfirmDialog` explains the denial. `needs_account`
confirms to Login; membership reasons confirm to the Membership screen. Copy comes from
`membershipGateCopy` (exhaustive on `AccessDenialReason`). Do not park an inline
"Account required" card (`GatedFeatureNotice`) above a button the user has not tapped.

The exception is a **fill empty**: the whole body is missing because the feature requires an
account (Library history, playlists). That still uses **`CallToActionSection`** below.

Helper copy that is not the content itself (directory explainer, why-add notes) uses
**`HelperNote`** — tertiary fill and a leading info icon — so it does not read as a description.

## Login-gated fill states

When a screen's body is empty because the feature requires an account, use **`CallToActionSection`**
(it already wraps `VerticalCenter`) plus a Login action — not a bare `ListEmpty`. Prefer
**`AuthAwareLoadState`** with `showAuthRequired` (it defaults to `authentication.login_required`);
otherwise wire `CallToActionSection` as the `FillList` empty (or the only `MobileScreenContainer`
child).

The body is the generic login-required sentence — see **generic-login-required-copy**. Hide the
in-body heading on that fill — the `HeaderBar` title is enough.

## Login / Sign up overlay

Login and Sign up slide up as a full-screen `Modal` over the tab shell — they must not replace
the navigator. Dismiss with a down chevron (`HeaderBarChrome` `backIcon="chevron-down"`,
`testID="auth-dismiss"`). Do not add a Cancel button. The account switch is body text plus a
link-style `Pressable` under Submit (`auth-switch-signup` / `auth-switch-login`).

## Do not

- Use a different page gutter (`md`, `2xl`, raw numbers) for the body under `HeaderBar`.
- Rebuild the title-bar height or type in a screen-local `StyleSheet`.
- Add a divider, hairline, or shadow under `HeaderBar`.
- Put a second in-body display heading on a screen that already has a `HeaderBar` title.
- Use raw `FlatList` for a screen list that shows a `VerticalCenter` fill empty, then hand-toggle
  `scrollEnabled` / `bounces` at the screen.
- Leave a bottom hairline on the last list row, or drop media-row vertical padding back to
  `spacing.md`.

